   "id": "a1-01",
   "level": "A1",
   "title": "Hello!",
   "he": "שָׁלוֹם",
   "intro": "<p>Your first words. <b>שָׁלוֹם</b> means hello, goodbye and peace. Israelis are informal: a quick <b>מָה נִשְׁמָע?</b> (what's up?) is the normal greeting, and <b>בְּסֵדֶר</b> or <b>הַכּוֹל טוֹב</b> is the normal answer.</p><p>Hebrew has no word for \"is\" or \"am\" in the present: <b>אֲנִי דָּנָה</b> = I (am) Dana.</p>",
