   "he": "רוֹצֶה, אוֹהֵב, יֵשׁ לִי",
   "intro": "<p>Your first verbs. In the present tense a verb has <b>four forms</b> — like an adjective: <b>רוֹצֶה / רוֹצָה / רוֹצִים / רוֹצוֹת</b>. Pick by who's speaking or being talked about.</p><p>\"I have\" is <b>יֵשׁ לִי</b> (lit. there is to me), and the casual \"I feel like…\" is <b>בָּא לִי</b>.</p><p>You also meet the first two verbs of the <a href=\"#/verbs\">verb course</a>: <b>לִקְנוֹת</b> (to buy) and <b>לָגוּר</b> (to live).</p>",
